comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T15:16:35.016Z",codex-agent,"Carried forward branch evidence from 2026-11-06T12:10:38.120Z (codex-sol): Reusing this issue owner for gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 in the G2 adoption PR, linked to pm-csv-sdk-write-fence and companion pm-cli-website-sumw. Activate the explicit target workspace and use its public active type/field registrations in admission, revision reads and compensation; cover real installed schema extensions and cross-workspace isolation."
  "2026-11-09T15:16:36.012Z",codex-agent,"Carried forward branch evidence from 2026-11-06T12:33:57.172Z (codex-sol): Validation: six real installed-extension tests pass, covering TOON and JSON Markdown source documents, strict unknown-field policy, direct and host-injected admission, cross-workspace isolation, separate-CLI revision conflicts and interrupted representation replay with opaque string/object fields. Disposable admission registry-only revert fails all five admission/isolation tests; omitting registered fields only from representation parsing fails the recovery test. Restored implementation passes 6/6. Existing resource-bound, late-invalid-row, source/settings and revision scenarios remain covered."
  "2026-11-09T15:16:36.937Z",codex-agent,"Carried forward branch evidence from 2026-11-06T16:50:57.780Z (codex-sol): Review round 2 extends the installed-registry fix to direct spreadsheet export/apply and atomic imports without admission. Admitted imports now pass target-check callbacks through one public SDK extension scope instead of reactivating on every revision/sequence read; standalone checks still activate explicitly. Real extension fixtures count lifecycle activations and preserve opaque string/object fields under strict schema policy. Initial new tests exposed a legacy transport assertion that incorrectly counted its CLI subprocess activations; restrict that bound to admitted in-process checks and retain legacy field-preservation assertions."
  "2026-11-09T15:16:37.873Z",codex-agent,"Carried forward branch evidence from 2026-11-06T17:00:15.093Z (codex-sol): Round 2 final linked validation passes 14/14 installed-extension tests, including direct spreadsheet export/apply in TOON and JSON Markdown, non-admitted atomic field preservation, repeated admitted target checks, standalone revision/sequence activation, existing replay/recovery and workspace isolation. New regressions use real SDK trackers and installed schema extensions. All five isolated behavioral reverts fail; restored new cases pass 5/5. Review threads PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s60lXG2 and PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s60lXHD will be answered after the fix push. Fresh current-head CI and full review remain required."
  "2026-11-09T15:16:38.879Z",codex-agent,"Carried forward branch evidence from 2026-11-06T21:35:23.416Z (codex-sol): Round 3 lineage fix validation: linked installed-extension suite passes 16/16; existing lineage suite passes 4/4 including concurrent native creation and replay. Exact pre-fix importLineage reversion fails both registered-type cases (0/2) after native creation; exact pre-fix existingRow reversion fails both replay cases (0/2). Fixed SDK activation remains live through receipt construction, and native folder lookup uses active SDK registrations. Real strict-schema fixtures preserve opaque native defaults and item/history identity in TOON and JSON Markdown trackers. Restored targeted cases pass 5/5. Main reconciliation changes only toolchain dependencies, retaining audited SDK 2026.11.5 and taking main pm-ops 2026.11.2; no PM histories were merged or rewritten."
  "2026-11-09T15:30:46.175Z",codex-agent,"PR #231 continuation preserves the installed-registry fix while strengthening activation lifecycle evidence: four direct/command cases assert one activation across native TOON and JSON Markdown; generated nested admission/revision/spreadsheet/join previews reuse the scope. Disabling only reuse fails 0/6 selected cases; restoration passes. Linked admission/join tests pass 27/27, broader focused tests 92/92, packed npm/Bun acceptance all eight scenarios. Main history prefix is retained and prior branch comments/files/docs/tests were re-recorded with pinned pm after merging main. Current full release certification remains with PR CI under the supplied local time limit."
